        "November 20, 2025 status request (evidence of reliance on representations)",
        "Rojo's delayed response and non-appearance (Nov. 20, 2025)",
        "Rojo's arrival at Plaintiff's residence as family was departing (Nov. 21, 2025) — evidence of intentional timing",
        "Rojo's denial statement citing unwritten office policy limiting travel to 'emergency or death in family'",
        "Evidence that alleged policy appears nowhere in CDCR's published parole conditions",
        "Rojo's new citation of ankle monitor justification — previously unraised during multi-day communications",
        "Evidence that ankle monitor had never previously been cited as impediment to travel",
        "Evidence of secular travel approvals under comparable or less restrictive circumstances (disparate treatment)",
        "2021 approval of identical church travel to Reno under different supervising agent (relevant comparator)",
        "CDCR published parole travel requirements (establishing compliance)",
        "CDCR published list of legitimate parolee travel restrictions (demonstrating absence of religious carve-out)"
